    "beamjoy.window.config.tabs.core.legacyImport.races.invalidTag": "couldn't be converted",
    "beamjoy.window.config.tabs.core.legacyImport.help.button": "How to install legacy races",
    "beamjoy.window.config.tabs.core.legacyImport.help.text": "Legacy Import brings Hunter arenas, Infected arenas, and races over from an old BeamJoy Free (BJI) server, so you don't have to rebuild them by hand.\n\nHow to install:\n1. On your OLD BeamJoy Free server, find its data folder's own \"scenarii\" subfolder at Resources/BeamJoyData/db/\n2. Copy that whole \"scenarii\" folder into THIS server's own Resources/BeamJoyData/db/ folder, so you end up with Resources/BeamJoyData/db/scenarii/<map>_hunter.json and/or <map>_races.json files.\n3. Restart this server with the new files, then click the button for whichever you want to import below.\n4. A preview lists every map found, with counts and any conflicts, before anything is actually imported. Nothing happens until you confirm it.\n\nHunter and Infected arenas import ONE PER MAP each and will OVERWRITE this fork's existing arena for any map that already has one. Both read the SAME <map>_hunter.json files (BJI stores both modes' spawn points together), so importing one doesn't consume or affect the other.\n\nRaces are different: every convertible race is added as a brand-new race, never overwriting anything already in your list. A race whose name is already used is skipped instead, so importing is always safe to re-run.",
